 ## [Unreleased]

+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool input against each tool's declared `inputSchema` before
+  invoking the executor, and `ToolRegistry.register` compiles static schemas up front so an invalid
+  schema fails at startup rather than mid-conversation. A rejected call returns a descriptive
+  `ToolResponse` to the model — naming the failing property path and constraint, never the offending
+  value — instead of throwing, so the model can correct the call within the existing tool-round
+  budget. Undeclared extra properties still pass through to the executor unchanged. **Migration
+  note:** an executor that previously hand-validated its input now receives only input the declared
+  schema accepts; a tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its own error message no
+  longer sees it.
+
 ## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-17

 ### Changed
